# skills.lock.json pins a SHA-256 of each skill's raw bytes, so a CRLF
# checkout (core.autocrlf on Windows) fails Aria Code's integrity check and no
# skill can activate automatically. Keep text LF in the repo and working trees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats: never touch line endings. text=auto already detects binary
# content; these make the intent explicit for files a skill may add later.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tgz  binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mov  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.otf  binary
